TERMS AND CONDITIONS

1. GRANT OF RIGHTS

   Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy
   of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to:

   a) USE the Software for any purpose, including commercial and private use,
      without restriction.

   b) MODIFY the Software for private or internal use.

   c) CONTRIBUTE modifications back to the official Sylph repository
      (the "Official Repository") via pull requests or other contribution
      mechanisms established by the project maintainers.

2. RESTRICTIONS

   The following actions are expressly PROHIBITED without prior written
   permission from the project maintainers:

   a) REDISTRIBUTION — You may NOT redistribute the Software, in whole or in
      part, in original or modified form, through any medium, including but not
      limited to: publishing forks, hosting mirrors, bundling with other
      software, or distributing compiled binaries derived from the Software.

   b) DERIVATIVE DISTRIBUTION — You may NOT distribute derivative works based
      on the Software. Modified versions are for private/internal use only.
      Public distribution of modifications must be contributed to the Official
      Repository.

   c) SUB-LICENSING — You may NOT grant rights to the Software to third parties
      beyond what is permitted in Section 1.

3. RATIONALE

   Sylph operates a peer-to-peer federated learning network that interconnects
   potentially millions of nodes. Unauthorized redistributions and modified
   forks pose critical security risks to all participants in the network,
   including but not limited to:

   - Introduction of backdoored or poisoned model weights
   - Bypass of Byzantine fault tolerance and validation mechanisms
   - Compromise of differential privacy guarantees
   - Sybil attacks through unvetted client modifications
   - Network fragmentation undermining collective intelligence

   All modifications to the Software that affect network-facing behavior MUST
   be reviewed and merged through the Official Repository to maintain the
   security and integrity of the global Sylph network.

   NOTE: Security of the P2P network against modified clients is enforced
   technically, not solely legally. Technical enforcement mechanisms include:
   (1) 6-stage cryptographic validation of every received LoRA delta,
   (2) code-signed release verification in the installer,
   (3) Byzantine aggregation that rejects deltas from poorly-behaved nodes
       regardless of what software they claim to run.
   The no-redistribution clause reinforces this technical enforcement.

4. CONTRIBUTIONS

   By submitting contributions to the Official Repository, you agree that your
   contributions are licensed under the same terms as this license.

5. DISCLAIMER

   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
